  "verbalization": "Leuconodine E appears to have multiple pathways leading to NCI-H446, suggesting a potential mechanism of action involving protein-tyrosine phosphatase LC-PTP and Npc15336. The first pathway links leuconodine E to JM1, which is targeted by hexadecanedioic acid, and ultimately to NCI-H446. The second pathway directly connects leuconodine E to Protein-tyrosine phosphatase LC-PTP, which is then targeted by a complex compound, and finally to NCI-H446. The third pathway also connects leuconodine E to Protein-tyrosine phosphatase LC-PTP, which is targeted by Npc15336, and again to NCI-H446. These findings suggest that leuconodine E may act through a series of molecular interactions involving phosphatase activity, potentially modulating signaling pathways in NCI-H446 cells. The evidence supports a mechanistic link between leuconodine E and NCI-H446, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
